 "traps": [
  "the repository is a dotnet new template: <!--#if (UsePostgreSQL)--> and #if (UseSqlServer) blocks are XML or C# comments in the committed files, so all three databases, both clients and their packages are present at this commit",
  "the two clients have the same npm name cleanarchitecture.web: they are referred to by root, src/Web/ClientApp (Angular) and src/Web/ClientApp-React (React with Vite)",
  "Angular is attributed to the angular.json project CleanArchitecture.Web; Vitest runs through @angular/build:unit-test of that project",
  "the .NET units are named after their .csproj files (Web, Infrastructure, AppHost), not after their AssemblyName (CleanArchitecture.Web, ...)",
  "PostgreSQL and SQL Server come from Aspire's Azure resources (AddAzurePostgresFlexibleServer, AddAzureSqlServer) that run as containers locally; SQLite is the default connection string",
  "Azure Key Vault is used only when AZURE_KEY_VAULT_ENDPOINT is set; Azure Container Apps is the Aspire deployment target",
  "NUnit is written nunit in four test projects and NUnit in one; Moq, Shouldly and Respawn are test helpers, and MediatR, AutoMapper and FluentValidation are libraries outside the listed classes",
  "only frameworks and services are measured; the other facets are in unknown"
 ],
